Package: hadith
Architecture: all
Depends:
 fortune-mod,
 fortunes-hadith (= ${source:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: sayings of the Prophet Muhammad(saw), in the shape of fortune
 hadith prints a saying of the Prophet Muhammad(saw), chosen at random, the way
 fortune(6) prints a cookie. Run from a shell profile it gives one saying a
 login; run with -m it is a plain-text search over the corpus.
 .
 The corpus is "The Sayings of Muhammad", collected and translated by Abdullah
 al-Mamun al-Suhrawardy and published in 1905: 439 sayings arranged over 85
 topics, plus four the book prints in its preamble. It is in the public domain
 in the United States and in Europe.
 .
 This package is the command. The sayings themselves are in fortunes-hadith,
 which can also be installed on its own if all you want is for fortune(6) to
 draw from them along with everything else.

Package: fortunes-hadith
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 fortune-mod,
Description: sayings of the Prophet Muhammad(saw) - data files for fortune
 Two fortune(6) cookie files holding "The Sayings of Muhammad", collected and
 translated by Abdullah al-Mamun al-Suhrawardy and published in 1905: 439
 sayings arranged over 85 topics, plus four the book prints in its preamble.
 It is in the public domain in the United States and in Europe.
 .
 The sayings are installed twice. hadith-suhrawardy is a modernisation of
 Suhrawardy's Victorian English - "pays" for "payeth", "you" for "thou" - made
 so that they read as living language rather than as a museum piece.
 hadith-suhrawardy-1905 is the original wording unaltered, installed beside it
 so that every change made stays a diff a reader can check.
 .
 Installing this package alone is enough for fortune(6) to draw from them. The
 hadith package adds a command that draws from these two corpora only, and
 makes the modernised text the default.
